<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Koki</h1><p class="st-meta">1740 CE – 1896 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small kingdom west of Lake Victoria, founded by a prince of Bunyoro and absorbed into Buganda in 1896.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tradition says Koki was founded around 1740 by Bwohe, a prince of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bunyoro">Kingdom of Bunyoro</a>, who settled in the lands west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-victoria">Lake Victoria</a> in today's Rakai district. It lay between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-buganda">Buganda</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ankole">Ankole</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haya-people">Haya</a> kingdoms.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Koki was a small farming and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>-keeping kingdom, ruled by a king, or kamuswaga, through chiefs. From around 1800 it paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-buganda">Kingdom of Buganda</a> while keeping its own dynasty, and it took part in the trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and iron goods around the lake.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1896 Koki's ruler agreed to incorporation into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-buganda">Buganda</a>, and it became a county of the kingdom under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/uganda-protectorate">Uganda Protectorate</a>, its ruler keeping the title kamuswaga. It remains part of the Buganda region today.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1740 CE – 1896 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Horn and East Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.33%;width:3.10%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1740 CE – 1896 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Luganda</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uganda">Uganda</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Koki</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1818&amp;focus=kingdom-of-koki" aria-label="Kingdom of Koki on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5596 2096 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Koki lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5900 2421h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5916 2352h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5916 2352h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Uganda. <a href="/atlas?year=1818&amp;focus=kingdom-of-koki">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
